From 56ad05a578d4cebc16bd08fe8128f28598a37d6b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Timothy Tan <2604749@sit.singaporetech.edu.sg>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 18:43:07 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Web app: readable decision pages and a consistent style

- The audit page shows the decision in plain English with a colour for the
  outcome (green approved, amber review, red rejected), the approved subsidy,
  SME and audit-passed flags, and the matched schemes, reasons and
  recommendations as lists. The AI audit, the application and the thresholds
  the decision used are labelled tables; the raw JSON is still there, folded.
- History lists each audit with a coloured decision badge and the subsidy.
- 'Run AI/Logic Manager (only)' use the same panel and table.
- web/display.py holds the presentation helpers (labels, tones, money,
  labelled rows); it decides nothing.
- One stylesheet in base.html: header bar, cards, buttons, form fields and
  tables, readable on a phone. The register page states the account rules.
- Tests in tests/test_web_display.py.
